Fillets and chamfers: on a closed line of the other contact, the parameters
of a gap's crossings in the period that follows the piece before the gap
(mitcad#495).

The case: a plate's corner rounded with radius 20 about the axis of a boss
of radius 7.5 under it, a side of the plate tangent to the corner's arc
(not square to the boss's seam), the boss's foot chamfered by 13 so that
the contact on the plate's underside (radius 20.5) runs 0.5 beyond the
plate's outline along the corner and both sides (patch 0142's gap, cut by
a chain of the faces beyond). The boss's seam, the closed spine's start,
lies before the gap (a little short of where the gap ends, going along the
spine), so the gap is long and ends towards the spine's end.
ChFi3d_KPartEdgeCrossing takes a crossing's parameter on the other
contact's line (a circle on the boss) in the period around the middle of
the piece before the gap: past half a turn from there, a period early
(-0.286 for 5.997). The last piece of the chain, from that crossing to the
next piece's start (6.218), then ran more than once round the circle: the
boss's bottom face got edges covering more than its rim, the cone's seam a
tolerance of 58 mm, and the result was invalid (when the boss was as long
as the chamfer, its bottom face's repair then never ended, patch 0942).

ChFi3d_KPartChainPieces now takes each crossing's parameter in the period
that follows the end of the piece before the gap (or the chain's given
start), where the gap does not run across the spine's start (the
parameters grow along the spine); a gap across the start keeps the
parameters as before (0145 and 0146 take them across the period's end).

On the design's replayed body before the item: valid, the four bosses'
chamfers the change of volume of the file's (+25112.58 against
+25112.65 mm3, the replayed body itself 0.067 mm3 off the stored one);
before, invalid (two of the four wrong by +618 and -733 mm3). Synthetic:
the plate and boss of the case (the boss 15 long), the boss's seam turned
in steps of 15 degrees: valid, the volume of the boss with the chamfer's
cone cut by the plate's outline within 1e-6 mm3; before, invalid for the
seam from 120 to 180 degrees.

Upstream: new.
